I load the profile pointer once and add GCC branch hints so the common valid path stays straight-line. This reduces redundant loads and improves branch layout without changing behavior.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    auto p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    if (__builtin_expect(profileIndex < p->numFields, 1))
        return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```